in ancient times the god emperor of UT  was amongst the most powerful rulers in  all the known world the Empire was  prosperous with wealth that surpassed  even Valyria at its peak the vast empire  stretched from the bone mountains all  the way to the Jade Sea and was ruled by  the one true God on earth son of the  maiden of the light and the Lion of  night he was called the Emperor of the  dawn for ten thousand years he reigned  and for ten thousand years et prospered  according to the world of Ice and Fire  et is believed by some to be one of the  first places were mankind climbed out of  the pit of savagery and into  civilization et was one of the first  places to have towns and cities and also  one of the first to develop a system of  writing if legend can be believed the  wealth of UT was such that its princes  lived in houses of solid gold its cities  were grand spectacles larger than any  found in the West and he teased armies  were vast thought to be of nearly  unimaginable size et itself was a vast  Kingdom full of rolling hills deep Lakes  jungles and mighty forests all bound  together under the rule of the dawn  Emperor it is said that the Emperor of  the dawn wondered his kingdom in a  Polock and carved from a single giant  pearl hosts it up by his 100 Queens at  the end of his reign legend tells us  that the Emperor of the dawn ascended  into the stars leaving dominion of his  realm to his eldest son who was named  the Pearl Emperor during the millennia  that followed the dawn Emperor's death  each Emperor's reign was more troubled  and shorter than the last and according  to the world of Ice and Fire baleful  beasts pressed at the borders of their  empire ut became more chaotic as lesser  Kings grew prideful and rebellion rang  out through the lands it is said that  the people of ET had changed giving  themselves over to lust gluttony murder  and sloth at the height of these  troubles the amethyst Empress was slain  by her own brother who then called  himself the bloodstone Emperor  he usurped his sister and ushered in a  new era of Darkness but why  what corrupted ET to the point of  anarchy and kin slaying to find the  answer we have to dig deeper the world  of Ice and Fire tells us that the  bloodstone Emperor worship the black  stone that fell from the sky but it does  not in fact tell us when this black  stone arrived the stone could have very  well existed since the ascension of the  dawn Emperor the stone itself is clearly  a reference to the work of Lovecraft it  is otherworldly and is known to cause  terrifying dreams that can lead to  madness the black stone is mentioned  multiple times in our story including  but not limited to the sea stone chair  the monument of Toad Isle and the base  of the high tower at Old Town it would  seem that the arrival of the bloodstone  Emperor's stone correlates with the  descent of Yi T into chaos and darkness  it is known that during his reign the  bloodstone Emperor practiced many dark  arts including torture and necromancy  not unlike many still do in a shy until  this very day in fact the practices of  the bloodstone Emperor aligned well with  modern day practices and a shy ash I  itself is made entirely of the same  black stone and no magic is forbidden in  a shy even magic that requires the  extraction of human life so is there  something about the black stone that  causes people to become mad or perhaps  obsessed with dark magic beyond Yi T's  fabled five forts hiding in the frozen  gray wastes  waits the haunted city of Kadath it is  said that qaddafi is a place where  unspeakable rites are taking place all  in the name of ancient mad gods and  upriver through the heart of darkness  past a shy  lies the dark city of stag I were no man  dare venture boast a guy and Kadath are  loved craft references both our ancient  places where malevolent gods live it is  also common in Lovecraft's work for  sleeping or dormant gods such as Cthulhu  to send dreams into the minds of  humanity leading to chaos and sometimes  insanity  with all this considered the bloodstone  Emperor's black stone could possibly  mark the arrival of these deities the  baleful beasts mentioned earlier could  refer to these gods or their minions of  course so-called gods and Lovecraftian  lore are really just supreme beings far  surpassing the intelligence of people  humans are inconsequential to them and  merely tolerated I would argue that  there is evidence that such beings exist  in martens universe as well although  they are far more abstract affecting the  world only through suggestion was the  bloodstone Emperor corrupted by such  beings it is believed by many and Yi T  that the bloodstone Emperor's actions  led directly to the event which is now  known as the long night a period of time  where darkness ruled for generation the  world of Ice and Fire also counts the  bloodstone Emperor as the first high  priest of the starry wisdom a nefarious  cult the name is again borrowed directly  from Lovecraft in his lore the Church of  the starry wisdom worships Nyarlathotep  also known as the chaos King so we have  a mysterious insidious black stone a  malevolent old city hiding in a frozen  desert and a baleful cult that worships  a god of chaos all of which would be  expected if Lovecraftian type entities  were present in the isang of Ice and  Fire universe and since it was the  bloodstone Emperor's worship of the  black stone and his other dark practices  that were believed to have brought about  the long night does that mean that it  was the will of these so-called gods  there are multiple places in A Song of  Ice and Fire where these entities seem  likely to reside including Stagg I and  the heart of winter as I discussed in my  video on ash I Kadath is another which  makes even more sense considering its  proximity to ET could the being at Kedah  have been responsible for the fall of  the dawn Empire and perhaps even the  long night itself  if so then why  well beings of chaos hold the name for a  reason they are a source of fear and  dread in humans and cause anxiety and  mistrust amongst mankind the people of  ET hold that the world was a broken  place after the long night  to quote the world of ice and fire  directly yet the great Empire of the  dawn was not reborn for the restored  world was a broken place where every  tribe of men when its own way fearful of  all the others and war and lust and  murder endured even to our present day  or so the men and women of the further  east believed  modernity is a grand kingdom of ruins  were a hundred Prince's and three  emperors can test for power all ruling  as they please within their own domains  and so UT the once great single Empire  is now divided and chaotic was it the  simple natural course of entropy or was  it the will of nefarious beings from  beyond the stars to take no mind to the  lesser beings that get in the way of  their sport there is no actual way to  know for sure  these events are some of the oldest in  the history of the world bison fire ET  was old before men ever ventured west  all we can say for sure is that Martin  has made very clear references to H P  Lovecraft's mythos especially in regards  to the black stone madness and chaotic  gods but we will likely never know for  certain thank you guys for watching make  sure you like and subscribe for more  ideas of Ice and Fire
 

